Subject: Cantor Schema-Pinned In-Domain Calibration Justification

@ [justification_uuid] b6280c9c-ad7c-4a2d-862e-e6f54a488e15
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Schema_Pinned_In_Domain_Calibration.sop

& [Problem] is a calibration type-system gap
  + structurally shaped expected arguments can still contradict the deployed procedure schema
  + the first corpus mixed unsupported subjects into positive accuracy denominators

& [Decision] is schema compilation before measurement
  + pin a reviewed contract snapshot to the catalogue digest
  + validate every expected positive through its exact closed schema
  + run a new subject-Cantor-only adaptive corpus and preserve its status honestly

& [Value] is a meaningful measurement denominator
  + routing and extraction outcomes are compared only to executable expectations
  + other-faculty prompts become explicit negative boundary controls
  + future contract expansions will require new snapshots and corpus identities

& [Rejected] remains explicit
  + changing the old corpus would destroy evidence history
  + expanding the runtime to other faculties merely to fit a test would reverse authority
  + omitting the adaptive label would overstate confirmation strength
